==English==

===Etymology===
{| style="float: right"
|-
|{{PIE word|en|só}}
|{{PIE word|en|úd}}
|}
{{root|en|ine-pro|*h₂en-|*h₁ep-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|ther-aboute}}, {{m|enm|ther-abouten|t=of a place or an object: around there, in its vicinity; surrounding it; nearby, neighbouring; here and there, throughout that place; of an action, matter, etc.: about, concerning; of an amount or distance: approximately, more or less; of time: about then, around that time}}{{nb...|therabouʒtte, there a-bowtyn, thorbuten, þare aboute, þare a-bouten, (Early Middle English) þarabutan, þær abuton|otherforms=1}},<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=thē̆r-abǒute(n|pos=adv|id=MED45142}}</ref> from {{inh|en|ang|þǣr-ābūtan}}, {{m|ang|þǣr-onbūtan}}, from {{m|ang|þǣr|t=there}} (ultimately from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*só|t=this; that}} + {{m|ine-pro|*-r}}) + {{m|ang|abūtan}}, {{m|ang|onbūtan|t=about; round about; on; on the outside}} (from {{m|ang|on-|pos={{glossary|prefix}} meaning ‘on; upon; there; thither; to’}} (ultimately from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*h₂en-|t=on; onto}}) + {{m|ang|būtan|t=just, merely, only}} (ultimately from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*h₁ep-}} + {{m|ine-pro|*úd|t=away; out; outwards; upwards}})). The English word is analysable as {{m|en|there}} + {{m|en|about}}.<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=adv|id=200472|date=June 2021|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|entry=thereabouts|alt=thereabouts ''(also'' thereabout'')''|pos=adv}}</ref>

The word is attested earlier than {{m|en|thereabouts}}.

